  "key_results": [
    "TDC states were 75–125 bar and 780–920 K with fixed 2000 bar diesel and 330 bar gas injection.",
    "Gas-jet soot luminosity generally began only after peak heat release; ending injection before that peak could prevent visible sooting."
  ],
  "mechanisms": [
    "Ambient reactivity controls pilot ignition delay; geometry and timing then determine whether gas disrupts or couples to the pilot."
  ],
